                  "type": "raw",
                  "value": "<h2>References</h2><div class=\"csl-bib-body\">\n  <div id=\"ref-CaldwellHarris2023\" data-csl-entry-id=\"CaldwellHarris2023\" class=\"csl-entry\">Caldwell-Harris, C. L. (2023). Understanding the Autistic Experience. <i>Current Opinion in Psychology</i>, <i>52</i>, 101624. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.copsyc.2023.101624</div>\n  <div id=\"ref-GillespieLynch2017\" data-csl-entry-id=\"GillespieLynch2017\" class=\"csl-entry\">Gillespie-Lynch, K., Brooks, P. J., Someki, F., Obeid, R., Shane-Simpson, C., Kapp, S. K., Daou, N., &#38; Smith, D. S. (2017). Changing College Students’ Conceptions of Autism: An Online Training to Increase Knowledge and Decrease Stigma. In <i>Autism in Adulthood</i> (Vol. 1, pp. 56–66). Mary Ann Liebert.</div>\n  <div id=\"ref-Loomes2017\" data-csl-entry-id=\"Loomes2017\" class=\"csl-entry\">Loomes, R., Hull, L., &#38; Mandy, W. P. L. (2017). What is the Male-to-Female Ratio in Autism Spectrum Disorder? A Systematic Review and Meta-Analysis. <i>Journal of the American Academy of Child &#38; Adolescent Psychiatry</i>, <i>56</i>(6), 466–474. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jaac.2017.03.013</div>\n  <div id=\"ref-Mantzalas2022\" data-csl-entry-id=\"Mantzalas2022\" class=\"csl-entry\">Mantzalas, J., Richdale, A. L., &#38; Dissanayake, C. (2022). A Conceptual Model of Risk and Protective Factors for Autistic Burnout. <i>Autism in Adulthood</i>, <i>4</i>(1), 1–12. https://doi.org/10.1089/aut.2021.0053</div>\n  <div id=\"ref-Pellicano2014\" data-csl-entry-id=\"Pellicano2014\" class=\"csl-entry\">Pellicano, E., Dinsmore, A., &#38; Charman, T. (2014). What Should Autism Research Focus Upon? Community Views and Priorities from the United Kingdom. <i>Autism</i>, <i>18</i>(7), 756–770. https://doi.org/10.1177/1362361314529627</div>\n</div>"
